  "brief": "A FUNCTIONAL rolling monster truck (slug monster-truck, category vehicles): pickup silhouette ~12 in long x 9 in tall, rolling on wooden dowel axles. EXACTLY 6 part types, 6 steps, one refPart figure per step, round coordinates. PARTS: (1) 'body-core' — full pickup profile (long hood, cab with window hole, bed rail), 12 in long, STRAIGHT solid bottom edge with NO arch cutouts, count 24, laminate true (stacks to 3.6 in solid core, like commercial stacked-profile cardboard toys), with TWO round Ø0.31 in axle holes at (2.9, ~2.4 in above the bottom edge) and (9.1, same) — every layer identical. (2) 'side-skin' Truck Side Silhouette — same profile but WITH big wheel-arch openings: semicircle radius 2.7 centered exactly on each axle hole center plus straight legs down to the bottom edge; count 2, laminate true, NO axle holes (the arch is open there). (3) 'wheel-disc' — Ø4.75 in circle, count 36, laminate true, ONE round Ø0.26 in hub hole dead center (snug press-fit on the dowel), 8 scored diagonal tread slits around the rim; 9 discs glue into one 1.35 in thick wheel, four wheels. (4) 'wheel-face' — Ø4.75 in ring, Ø2.4 in center opening (recessed hub look), count 4. HARDWARE: one entry id 'axle-dowel', kind dowel, diameterIn 0.25, lengthIn 7.5, count 2, label '1/4-inch wooden dowel, 7.5 inches long'. MECHANISMS: two revolutes 'front-axle' and 'rear-axle', axle 'axle-dowel', bearings [{part body-core, hole 0}] resp hole 1, hubs [{part wheel-disc, hole 0}], spins listing every disc and face-ring instance of that end. ASSEMBLY (thicknessIn 0.15, ground y=0): 24 body-core instances pos [0,9,z] z=-1.8,-1.65,...,+1.65; side-skins at z=-1.95 (mirror true) and +1.8; per wheel 9 discs + 1 face ring stacked outboard from z=±2.05 with 0.1 in washer gap to the skin (front wheels pos x 0.525, rear 6.725, pos y 4.75); two hardware dowel instances pos [2.9,2.375,0] and [9.1,2.375,0] rot [0,90,0]. Axle holes land at world y 2.375 so Ø4.75 wheels touch the ground. fitChecks: core axle hole vs 0.25 dowel clearance +0.04..0.12; wheel-disc hub hole vs 0.25 dowel clearance 0..0.03; skin arch radius (length d from arch top to axle center) atLeast 2.625; wheel-face opening holeWidth atLeast 2.0; body-core width match side-skin width. STEPS (grown-up flags on knife/drill/dowel steps): print+trace; cut+score+punch holes; glue the 24-layer core using the dowels as alignment pins; glue a skin on each face; build four wheels (9 discs + face ring, hub holes lined up); push dowels through the core bearings and press+glue wheels onto the dowel ends only — wheels spin, truck rolls. Difficulty 3, 6+ with a grown-up, 2-3 hours. SPEED: hard 9-minute budget — decide geometry fast, round coordinates, compact JSON, terse instructions (2-3 per step), simple hero (4-6 paths). Start writing JSON early.",
